  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Bangalore-based Ujjivan started operations as a microfinance institution (MFI) in 2005 with the aim of providing financial services to the economically active poor.It currently operates across 24 states and union territories, and 209 districts across India, making it one of the largest MFIs in terms of geographical spread. It serves over 2.77 million active customers through 457 branches and directly employs over 10,000 staff.</narrative>
  </description>
